"2. ⟦CODE_0004⟧: 92 records, one callback every second record, so 46 callbacks and the run finishes. ⟦CODE_0005⟧: 45 callbacks, and it stalls. ⟦CODE_0006⟧ is the record number, so the last value in the finished run is 92 and ⟦CODE_0007⟧ shows it, while the machine has counted 46 hours. The check script says this as: last ⟦CODE_0008⟧ = ticks x K.\n"
"3. 260 blocks at ⟦CODE_0009⟧ are 65 records, so ⟦CODE_0010⟧ ticks. The same three cards, a total of 46, and 65 - 46 = 19 idle ticks. The tape is 65 × 2,048 = 133,120 bytes.\n"
